<Information title="About Keertana" breadcrumb="About" description="A multilingual library for discovering, reading, and preserving Christian worship songs and hymns.">
  <section aria-labelledby="why"><h2 id="why">Why Keertana exists</h2>
    <p>Worship songs can be hard to find when their lyrics are scattered across different places and languages. Keertana brings Telugu, Hindi, and English songs into an organized library, with a reading experience that respects each script.</p>
    <p>You can browse by language and starting letter, or search song titles in their original script or using Roman characters. You don’t need a Telugu or Hindi keyboard to begin looking for a song.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="mission"><h2 id="mission">Our mission</h2>
    <p>Help people find the words to Christian songs, sing praise, and worship God across languages. Keertana is a resource for discovering and reading songs, not a claim of authorship or ownership of the collection.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="vision"><h2 id="vision">The direction we’re working toward</h2>
    <p>A carefully organized multilingual library that becomes more useful through accurate lyrics, clearer sources, and thoughtful language support.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="library"><h2 id="library">How the library works</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Discover.</strong> Browse Telugu, Hindi, and English songs, or search by title and transliteration.</li>
      <li><strong>Read.</strong> Adjust the lyric size, copy the lyrics, or share a song link.</li>
      <li><strong>Return.</strong> Saved Songs and the eight most recent visits stay in this browser, without an account or synchronization between devices.</li>
      <li><strong>Improve.</strong> Contribution forms let you prepare a new song or a correction. Sending is not connected yet, so no contribution is currently received or added through those forms.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Published entries are maintained in the project’s collection. Reviewing sources and corrections is part of the intended contribution process; an automated publishing or dedicated review workflow is not in place.</p>
    <p>Visited pages and some site resources may be available offline once cached. A first visit does not download the entire song library for offline reading.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="attribution"><h2 id="attribution">Song information and attribution</h2>
    <p>All credit for the songs belongs to their respective authors, lyricists, composers, and rights holders. Keertana does not claim copyright ownership of the songs or lyrics displayed here. Individual credits have not yet been recorded in the collection; missing credits do not mean a song has no author or is free to reproduce.</p>
    <p>When known, source and author or composer information can be included in a prepared song contribution. Sharing a song with Keertana does not make the contributor its author.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="care"><h2 id="care">A library that can improve</h2>
    <p>Accurate lyrics, clear attribution, responsible contributions, and language-sensitive corrections are the standards we want to build toward. Entries and transliterations can contain mistakes; they should be checked against reliable sources where accuracy matters.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="community"><h2 id="community">Help build Keertana</h2>
    <p>Know a missing song, notice a correction, or enjoy proofreading, translation, transliteration, design, or development? Explore the <a href="/contribute/">contribution hub</a>.</p>
    <ul><li><a href="/contribute/submit/">Prepare a song contribution</a></li><li><a href="/contribute/report/">Prepare an error report</a></li><li><a href="/contribute/join/">Explore joining the team</a></li></ul>
    <p>The forms currently check your details only. Explore the available options on the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Information>
